    "summary": "High‑energy Europe ’72 show with soaring Dark Star and iconic Looks Like Rain",
    "blurb": "Features a smoking Dark Star that segues into Sugar Magnolia, a breathtaking pedal‑steel rendition of Looks Like Rain, and an explosive Good Lovin’/Caution sandwich. Jerry’s solos and Keith’s keyboards drive the high‑octane performance throughout both sets.",
    "review": "The Tivoli Theater show on April 14, 1972 captures the Dead at a creative peak during their European ’72 tour. From the opening set the band rolls tight through classics like \"Bertha\" and \"Playing In The Band,\" but it’s the second set that truly shines: a soaring Dark Star that flows seamlessly into Sugar Magnolia, followed by Jerry’s ethereal pedal‑steel on \"Looks Like Rain.\" The centerpiece is the marathon Good Lovin’/Caution jam – a thunderous, improvisational whirlwind that showcases Keith’s magical organ/piano work and Bill’s propulsive drumming. Throughout the night Jerry’s guitar and rare steel work are nothing short of transcendent, Phil locks in with a solid, melodic bass line, and Bob provides steady rhythm and spot‑on vocals. The performance is both tight and adventurous, delivering the high‑energy, exploratory spirit that defines this era.",
